'' linux-x86_64: what gcc writes -- the numbered in .init_array / .fini_array plus the
'' number, and the unnumbered LLVM list as declared. See the source.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target linux-x86_64 --emit-ir tests/codegen/src/structor-order.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: internal global ptr @"P200", section ".init_array.00200", align 8
'' EXPECT-OUT: internal global ptr @"P101", section ".init_array.00101", align 8
'' EXPECT-OUT: internal global ptr @"Q101", section ".fini_array.00101", align 8
'' EXPECT-OUT: @llvm.global_ctors = appending global [4 x { i32, ptr, ptr }] [{ i32, ptr, ptr } { i32 65535, ptr @"A1", ptr null }, { i32, ptr, ptr } { i32 65535, ptr @"B2", ptr null }, { i32, ptr, ptr } { i32 65535, ptr @"C3", ptr null }, { i32, ptr, ptr } { i32 65535, ptr @"P65535", ptr null }]
'' EXPECT-OUT: @llvm.global_dtors = appending global [2 x { i32, ptr, ptr }] [{ i32, ptr, ptr } { i32 65535, ptr @"D1", ptr null }, { i32, ptr, ptr } { i32 65535, ptr @"D2", ptr null }]
'' EXPECT-OUT: @llvm.used = appending global [3 x ptr]
